%% Dialog Dismissal — a dialog nobody answers gets cancelled, and the session is told
%% Esc only ever cancels. Screens that offer "No, exit" stay alert-only, because Esc would end the session.

sequenceDiagram
    participant Probe as pane-probe.ts
    participant Pane as tmux pane<br/>(Claude Code)
    participant Thread as util.ts safeSend<br/>(chat thread)
    participant Transport as bridge-transport.ts
    participant Session as Claude session

    Note over Probe,Pane: Pane idle 30s+ and an "Esc to cancel" footer<br/>seen with no live prompt on two probes
    Probe->>Pane: capture tail again

    alt Dialog already closed
        Note over Probe: Stop: Esc would interrupt a working turn
    else Screen offers "No, exit", or the keypress failed
        Note over Probe: Count the attempt (10m cooldown, 3 max)
        Probe->>Thread: "is stuck on a dialog", tmux attach command
        Note over Probe,Session: Dialog stays up for a person. Session is not told.
    else Dialog still open
        Probe->>Pane: send-keys Escape
        Pane-->>Session: Dialog cancelled, not approved
        Note over Probe: Count the attempt (10m cooldown, 3 max)
        Probe->>Thread: "was stuck on a dialog", pressed Esc
        Thread-->>Probe: alert message id
        Note over Probe: A failed post is logged and does not stop the next step
        Probe->>Transport: notification: alert link, what it showed,<br/>rework or skip the step
        Transport->>Session: Delivered as a channel message
    end
